& [Solution]
  + one safe cantor_ecosystem kernel accepts an explicit Path plus strict marker commission and exact B2A receipt
  + it fully replays B2A before physical contact requires synthetic_fixture_only disposable fixture_only no live or cleanup authority and refuses any root-level .git link or reparse traversal
  + it reopens bounded raw source bytes verifies exact byte count and SHA256 validates the strict predecessor registry then deterministically constructs the successor snapshot registry record and receipt
  + persistence uses create_new in the exact final parent write_all file sync_all temporary reopen byte comparison same-volume rename replacement parent directory sync_all and final reopen parse digest and exact comparison
  + typed faults retain physical_contact replacement_performed and owned_temp_removed so a post-replacement failure cannot masquerade as atomic refusal or successful rollback

& [PlatformResult]
  + Ubuntu-24.04 WSL proves durable fixture persistence and a deterministic receipt awaiting boot validation
  + Windows proves safe replacement but parent-directory sync_all refuses Access Denied os error 5; the result is a typed post-replacement durability fault with success_receipt false

